# Local development settings for `mvn spring-boot:run`.
#
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# backend/.env is gitignored. The application reads it at startup, so these do not need
# exporting in every terminal. A real environment variable of the same name overrides the
# file, which is handy for a one-off.
#
# Read as a Java properties file: `export VAR=value` is not understood (use VAR=value), and
# a backslash in a value is an escape character (write it as \).
#
# Every value below is optional - the app runs with none of them, on H2 with a seeded
# owner account and the AI features switched off.

# --- AI features (summaries, Excel/smart import, statement screenshot import) ---
# Only the key is needed; the URL already defaults to Groq. Free key: https://console.groq.com/keys
INSIGHTS_API_KEY=
# INSIGHTS_API_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions
# INSIGHTS_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# INSIGHTS_VISION_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.6-27b

# --- Login ---
# Without these the seeded account is owner / ChangeMe123!
# OWNER_USERNAME=owner
# OWNER_PASSWORD=

# --- Secrets ---
# Optional locally: a development signing key is generated and reused from .dev-secrets/.
# Required under the prod profile, where startup fails without them.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48   and   openssl rand -base64 32
# JWT_SECRET=
# DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Biometric login ---
# WebAuthn needs a secure context; http://localhost qualifies, a plain-HTTP LAN address does not.
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost
# WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
